      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "A solid is a shape in three dimensions, and Render 3D is what makes it a picture: it shoots a ray from a camera through every pixel and lights what the ray lands on. The Master Gear turns the camera's Orbit once a loop, so the checker floor and the shadow swing round the ball. Drag the Sphere's Radius and Color, or unplug the Orbit and drag Orbit, Tilt and Distance on Render 3D yourself."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
